{
  "reason": "Select only model_design because positional embeddings are model-owned and all data, training, and evaluation components are frozen. The current validation HR@10 of 0.645, achieved at epoch 10 of 30, motivates testing whether substantial absolute-position signals impair generalization across sparse histories, but does not establish that hypothesis. Historical position-free NextItNet experiments support this ablation, while successful residual scaling supports preserving the current gated blocks and learned scales without introducing weight sharing or additional architectural changes.",
  "module": ["model_design"],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Remove self.pos_emb and its initialization from NextItNetModel.__init__, delete only the positions calculation inside encode_sequence, and replace x = self.dropout(x + self.pos_emb(positions)) * mask with x = self.dropout(x) * mask after the existing scaled item lookup, testing whether removing absolute interaction indices improves generalization while causal convolutions retain relative order. Preserve the eight independent blocks, dilation schedule [1,2,4,8,1,2,4,8], gated convolutions and gate initialization, normalization, dropout placement, trainable residual scales initialized to 0.1, item embedding initialization procedure, padding masks, final normalization, last-nonpadding selection, and tied item scoring; retain the unrelated positions variable in score_candidates. Keep MAXLEN=128, HIDDEN_UNITS=64, NUM_BLOCKS=8, KERNEL_SIZE=3, DROPOUT_RATE=0.2, LR=0.001, WEIGHT_DECAY=0.0, and BATCH_SIZE=128 unchanged. Preserve all remaining variable names and constructor, forward, encode_sequence, and score_candidates signatures, restricting source to the three permitted imports, eight numeric constants, and methods within NextItNetBlock and NextItNetModel, with no added file/network access, printing, training, evaluation, or CSV operations. Allocate one of the 44 candidate slots under the unchanged host protocol, preserving training seed 2024, validation negative-sampling seed 42, identical splits and candidates, BPR loss, Adam, clipping, 30 epochs, checkpoint selection, and score generation; retain the change only if host validation HR@10 exceeds 0.645, treating 0.655 as an experimental target and consulting no test metric.",
    "training_evaluation": null
  }
}
